ext4 file I/O: use the block cache for file data

lwext4 cached filesystem metadata but ext4_fread bypassed that cache for every
file-data read. Reopening an unchanged file therefore returned to the device,
and partial writes performed an uncached read-modify-write. Route reads and
partial writes through the existing coherent block cache. Keep the contiguous
full-block write path, invalidating any cached copies after it succeeds.

Covered by sw/userspace/storage's mount/write suite and the terminal gate,
which reads the device-request counter around two consecutive `ls` commands
and requires the second delta to be zero.

diff --git a/src/ext4.c b/src/ext4.c
--- a/src/ext4.c
